WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.480
One fertilized egg divides, and divides again.

2
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.240
The cells do not grow in between.

3
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.520
So where does the material for all those new cells come from?

4
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.900
It comes from the egg itself.

5
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.740
Cleavage is the run of rapid divisions after fertilization, and each small cell is a

6
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:28.200
blastomere. What does that do to the size of a cell, and to its membrane?

7
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.100
Here is a worked example, with invented round numbers.

8
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.020
Think of the zygote as one block of volume.

9
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.260
It holds 1.000 nL.

10
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.000
Each division doubles the count.

11
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.800
After five synchronous, equal divisions, with no growth and no cell loss, there are

12
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.380
two to the fifth power, which is 32 blastomeres.

13
00:00:53.183 --> 00:00:56.123
Volume is shared, not added.

14
00:00:56.823 --> 00:01:03.963
1.000 nL shared among 32 cells gives 31.25 pL for each cell.

15
00:01:04.623 --> 00:01:09.483
Add 32 cells of that size back up, and you get 1.000 nL again.

16
00:01:10.543 --> 00:01:14.083
Dividing made many cells, and made no new volume.

17
00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:18.587
Now the size. Take the cells as spheres.

18
00:01:19.407 --> 00:01:22.407
For a sphere, the diameter follows from the volume.

19
00:01:23.087 --> 00:01:26.867
The zygote is about 124 micrometres across.

20
00:01:27.647 --> 00:01:29.547
Each blastomere is about 39.

21
00:01:30.247 --> 00:01:35.047
That is smaller by the cube root of 32, which is 3.17.

22
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.950
Smaller cells carry more membrane.

23
00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:46.010
Added up, the 32 cells have about 3.17 times the membrane of the zygote.

24
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:52.270
Each division added cells and added membrane, but no new cytoplasm.

25
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:58.090
The number of nuclei rose 32-fold in the same cytoplasm.

26
00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:02.703
These numbers assume equal, synchronous divisions.

27
00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:05.543
A real mouse embryo breaks that.

28
00:02:06.203 --> 00:02:10.543
Its divisions are not synchronous, so counts need not be powers of two.

29
00:02:11.803 --> 00:02:15.883
Yolk matters too, because yolk slows or blocks the cleavage furrow.

30
00:02:16.743 --> 00:02:20.883
In birds, only a disc of cytoplasm on top of the yolk divides.

31
00:02:22.103 --> 00:02:28.123
Keep this rule. Cleavage divides without growth, so cells shrink while their number

32
00:02:28.123 --> 00:02:29.603
and total membrane rise.
